WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.940
In 1936, Congress set a rule
for federal flood projects.

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.570
A project could go ahead if the benefits,

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.490
to whomsoever they may accrue,

4
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.070
exceed the estimated costs.

5
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.940
Concrete has a price.

6
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.780
But what about cleaner air,

7
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.050
quiet streets, or fewer
deaths from pollution?

8
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.280
How can a government
put a price on cleaner

9
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.300
air before deciding
whether to build a road?

10
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.420
In this mission, you'll see
how economists turn a tiny

11
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.070
change in risk into a dollar figure.

12
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:33.520
Then you'll decide how much
cleanup is worth paying for,

13
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.370
one unit at a time.

14
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.240
Your mission: find out
how a dollar value is

15
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.280
put on things nobody buys.
